invariant: INV-14
file: handshake_parser_ee.c
catches: handshake_strict_webpki
reason: the TRUST=webpki EncryptedExtensions parser admits a server_name
  that carries data, where RFC 6066 §3 allows only the empty
  acknowledgement, so a body of the wrong length parses instead of
  failing as a decode error. bin/handshake_strict_webpki's server_name
  rows object.

--- old
    return ext == EXT_SERVER_NAME && ext_len == 0;
--- new
    (void)ext_len;
    return ext == EXT_SERVER_NAME;
